        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_988279885.1",
        "comments": "This project provides (pseudo-)haplotype one of the diploid genome assembly of the European hake, Merluccius merluccius, with a sample provided by Sissel Jentoft. The data generation and assembly were carried out by EBP-Nor (https://www.ebpnor.org/). The fMerMel2.1 assembly is based on 46x PromethION R10 Oxford Nanopore and 79x Arima Hi-C data. The ONT reads were assembled with hifiasm along with Hi-C data to generate a pair of haplotype-resolved assemblies. K-mers from the two assemblies were used to filter Hi-C reads to create two sets of reads for scaffolding the assemblies (i.e., reads used to scaffold hap1 did not contain k-mers unique to hap2). YaHS was used for scaffolding. FCS-adaptor was used to remove putative adapters, and putative contaminants were removed with FCS-GX. The chromosomes are ordered and oriented according to fMerMel1.",
